# Kinetic Platform skills

This is an optional, additive pointer — the portal in `portal/` runs fine
without it. If `ai-skills/skills/` exists in this repo (it's an optional
git submodule; see [ONBOARDING.md](../../ONBOARDING.md)), read the
relevant skill file(s) there before writing code that touches the Kinetic
Platform: forms, workflows, connections/operations, security policies, or
the platform REST API.

If `ai-skills/skills/` is empty or missing, the submodule hasn't been
initialized — that's a normal, supported state, not an error. Either
initialize it with `git submodule update --init ai-skills`, or proceed
without it.

## Which space

The Kinetic space this repo targets is `REACT_APP_PROXY_HOST` in
`portal/.env.development.local`. If a Kinetic MCP server is connected, it is
named `<space-slug>-kinetic` and serves that same space at
`/app/platform-ai/mcp`. Before any create, update or delete through it,
confirm which space you are on — say it back to the user if there is any doubt.
